              "sourceRegion": "Question 9a, lower-left triangle",
              "description": "Triangle ABC with A lower left, B lower right and C upper left; right-angle square at A, matching double ticks on AB and AC, AC labelled 1 and interior angle ABC labelled 45 degrees. Decorative blue outlines are reconstructed in black.",
              "mathematics": "AB = AC = 1; angle A = 90 degrees; angle B = 45 degrees. BC is the hypotenuse.",
              "answerVisibility": "All diagram labels and marks are permanent givens; the length BC is withheld."
